# Copy to .env and fill in. Gitignored.
# Generate at https://www.kaggle.com/settings/api -> "Generate New Token".
#
# ⚠️ ONE VARIABLE PER ACCOUNT, NAMED AFTER THAT ACCOUNT IN UPPER CASE:
#
#     KAGGLE_API_TOKEN_<USERNAME>=KGAT_xxxx
#
# `kgpu.accounts` takes the suffix, lower-cased, as the account's LABEL. The Kaggle SDK reads
# only the bare KAGGLE_API_TOKEN, so the chosen token is COPIED into it before the client
# authenticates -- which makes the choice this repo's, and not whichever variable happened to
# be called KAGGLE_API_TOKEN (`ACC-1`).
#
#     python -m kgpu accounts        every account here, with its remaining GPU hours
#     --account <label>              force one for any command
#
KAGGLE_API_TOKEN_YOURUSERNAME=

# A bare KAGGLE_API_TOKEN is still accepted -- it takes the label `default` -- but name it
# after its account instead: a token whose variable says one account and whose credentials
# say another is flagged by `kgpu accounts` and is how the wrong one gets picked by hand.

# Legacy alternative (older kaggle.json style):
# KAGGLE_USERNAME=
# KAGGLE_KEY=

# ⚠️ The REPO ROOT .env is loaded too, and after this one — so POSTGRES_* (which
# the export step needs) stays where it is, and the Kaggle token may live in
# either file. This one wins on a conflict.
